## Context
Child of tracker 1317 (forge leaks). The landing path is the highest-stakes surface: a raw
`gh` call here makes a no-forge or other-forge repository fail, or read "nothing found" as a
clear. Model: `scripts/forge.py` (gh and none backends, typed NOOP and refusal, offline cache),
`tests/test_forge.py`; the none backend's state is `review_notes.py` (refs/notes/review) and
`merge-gate.py` (refs/notes/gate).

Sites on main 2026-10-28:
- `skills/roar/close-and-clean.sh` (~342 `gh pr view --json state`, ~360 auto-merge armed read)
- `skills/roar/check-close-claims.sh` (~56 `gh pr list --state merged`)
- `scripts/check-cross-pr-ticket-collision.sh` (~100-133: open PR list, repo view, PR files)
- `scripts/review-anchor.py` (~31, error text naming `gh pr view`; check whether any raw call remains)

Shell callers need a CLI: today `forge.py` exposes only `resolve`. This child sets the CLI
shape (subcommands over the existing backend methods) that 1319 and 1320 build on.

Parent: tracker 1317.

## Plan (raid f7fa41: Imagine, Blind-Spot, feasibility PASS)
- Add three `forge.py` CLI subcommands, the whole tracker's CLI (1319 and 1320 consume them, never
  edit forge.py): `list --state open|merged|all [--head B] [--limit N]` (JSON rows fixed up front:
  number, branch, title, body, auto, mergedAt, cross_repository), `files <ref>`, `read-back <ref>`
  (exposes the existing verb: `STATE head queued|-`). No CLI per backend method.
- Backend routing for ref-less verbs (Blind-Spot 1): today `get_forge(ref="")` returns NoneForge
  even with gh installed (forge.py ~607, an empty ref is not numeric). A ref-less verb routes to gh
  when the repository has an origin remote and gh is on PATH.
- Three-row contract (Blind-Spot 2), mirroring `get_forge(landing=True)`'s `_has_origin` split:
  no origin remote → exit 3, typed NOOP "no forge" (stdout empty, never `[]`); origin but no gh,
  unauthed or unreachable → exit 2, could not look; origin with gh → the rows.
  The collision check may answer "skipped: no forge" exit 0 only on exit 3; on exit 2 it keeps its
  fail-closed exit 2. check-close-claims keeps its "NOT an all-clear" path.
- `read-back` reads with `landing=True` (no offline mark, no cache; Blind-Spot 3) and
  close-and-clean maps unreadable or exit 3 to today's COULD-NOT-LOOK (exit 2), never to a pass or
  a new KEEP-PENDING (pinned by tests/test_roar_close_and_clean.sh, tests/test_roar_armed_exit.py).
- review-anchor.py already resolves through forge (~29); only its error string (~31) names gh.
- Remove each ported site's `harness-extension-point` marker, so check-agnostic tells ported from
  residue (Blind-Spot 4).
- First test: `--forge none list --state open` in a repo with no origin and no gh exits 3 with
  empty stdout and "no forge" on stderr (catches the `[]`-and-exit-0 all-clear); second, an origin
  repo with no gh exits 2; third, a gh shim with an empty ref routes to gh.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The four sites above call `forge.py` (Python API or CLI) instead of `gh`, or are listed
      in this ticket's log as residue with a reason
- [ ] Each ported site has a `none`-backend test (no `gh` on PATH) showing the step still
      works or answers a typed NOOP/refusal, never an empty all-clear
- [ ] A verb or CLI subcommand is added to `scripts/forge.py` only where a caller here needs it,
      with its gh and none behaviour tested in `tests/test_forge.py`
- [ ] `make check` passes
